<http://data.silknow.org/object/d029a9fa-078b-3756-830c-a16908fae137/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Towel/Napkin, cotton embroidered with silk in double running variations and combinations and with metal thread in satin stitch filling in squares.\nEach end is bordered by a line of small motifs: a gold bowl with one floral spray of two blue flowers, two red leaves and one blue flower at the top.  Below this is a very narrow band of embroidered cypress trees alternating with two other stylised motifs.  The ends and lower sides of the towel are edged with metal and brown silk.\nOne side has been cut and hemmed."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d029a9fa-078b-3756-830c-a16908fae137> .

